+{"$schema":"fabro-journal-v1","run_id":"01M1RF53QWM4Q5REBVSG9F9Y43","node":"planner","visit":1,"status":"succeeded","ts":"2026-09-05T09:45:55Z","data":{"painpoints":[{"text":"Stage start was blocked by mise: every sd call failed with 'mise ERROR ... /repos/denkhaus/fabro/.mise.toml are not trusted' until I ran `mise trust` manually (this run, first two tool calls wasted). Known tracked painpoint fabro-66db covers run containers; the develop-stage planner hit the same wall here — evidence the fix should also cover in-repo stage shells."},{"text":"Planner's stale-basis check requires opening referenced files, but `read_file` on `.fabro/workflows/develop/prompts/implementer.md` is blocked by fs_hide for this stage ('path is hidden'); I had to fall back to shell grep/sed. If workflow prompts are intentionally hidden from the planner, the ADR-0015 stale-basis duty and the fs_hide policy conflict — worth a decision."}],"observations":["Stale-basis finding on fabro-37a6: a near-duplicate scripted-transform note landed at line ~25 of `.fabro/workflows/develop/prompts/implementer.md` in commit d9138572 (2026-09-04 06:07 UTC, fabro-5453 migration) BEFORE the seed was filed (23:01 UTC), citing the same incident with conflicting numbers (run 01M11P68SHFS: ~40 sites, 43%, 277 s vs seed's ~24 sites, 42%, 278 s); the seed's evidence ref fabro-28e8 does not resolve in the tracker. Brief resolves this as one in-place rewrite anchored on the verifiable run id.","Seed description contains a 'sd' typo for 'sed' and its perl-pinned claim is true (`.fabro/Dockerfile.toolchain:22` installs perl); fabro-4601 is confirmed a distinct mechanism (parallel edit_file serialization discipline), so the brief fences it out."]}}
